' 4+1 Scenarios (+1) - Catch / release a Pokémon (US01, US02)
' Version 1.0 - 2026-10-19 - reflects the current working tree
' Shows how the Logical view (HomeViewModel, PokemonRepository, CaughtPokemonEntity) and the Process view
' (Room as single source of truth, LiveData) support keeping the user's Pokédex up to date.
' Started here from HomeScreen; PokedexScreen (release only) and PokemonDetailScreen follow the same path.
' C4 equivalent: c4/dynamic-catch-release-pokemon.puml. Process detail: process-caught-state-sync.puml.
@startuml scenarios-catch-release
!include ../style.puml

title Scenario - catch / release a Pokémon
autonumber

actor User
participant HomeScreen
participant HomeViewModel
participant PokemonRepository
database "Local Database" as LocalDb

User -> HomeScreen : taps the star on a card
HomeScreen -> HomeViewModel : toggleCaught(pokemon)
alt not caught yet
    HomeViewModel -> PokemonRepository : catchPokemon(name, id)
    PokemonRepository -> LocalDb : insert caught_pokemon row
else already caught
    HomeViewModel -> PokemonRepository : releasePokemon(name)
    PokemonRepository -> LocalDb : delete caught_pokemon row
end
LocalDb --> HomeViewModel : caught list (Room LiveData)
HomeViewModel --> HomeScreen : caughtNames
HomeScreen --> User : star filled / empty
@enduml
